# Netlify publishes this whole folder, so anything sitting next to index.html is public.
# The game is index.html; everything else is repo housekeeping.
#
# The trailing "!" is REQUIRED. Without it Netlify serves the real file whenever one
# exists and never reaches the rule — which is exactly what happened on the first
# attempt. The force flag makes the redirect win over the static file.
/NOTES.md               /  301!
/README.md              /  301!
/OPERATING.md           /  301!
/validate-questions.js  /  301!
/database.rules.json    /  301!
/firebase.json          /  301!
/scripts/*              /  301!
